\title{polyDx: diagnostics for dominance-labelled variance in polyploid genomic prediction}
\description{
In autopolyploid genomic models the standard additive (A) and dominance (D)
relationship kernels built from a real marker matrix are nearly collinear
(A-D Frobenius cosine typically 0.91-0.98). Under that geometry the fitted
dominance share \eqn{V_D / (V_A + V_D)} sits near 0.5 even when the true
digenic dominance is exactly zero, so its magnitude is not evidence of
dominance. polyDx replaces "how big is the D share?" with a decision
procedure conditioned on each panel's own genotype matrix.
}
\section{Kernels}{

\code{\link{orthogonal_kernels}} and \code{\link{standard_kernels}} build the
orthogonal degree-wise and the standard VanRaden/digenic kernels from a
dosage matrix. \code{\link{build_panel}} builds both plus the matching
orthonormal contrast matrices, for fixed or per-marker variable ploidy.
}

\section{Diagnostic workflow}{

\code{\link{load_panel}} reads and QCs a panel; \code{\link{run_workflow_stage}}
runs one stage of the panel-conditioned battery (\code{geom}, \code{real},
\code{perm}, \code{addctrl}, \code{d2spike}, \code{structspike}, \code{pred});
\code{\link{workflow_scorecard}} applies the gates in
\code{\link{workflow_thresholds}} and returns a per-panel verdict.
}

